WEBVTT

00:03.390 --> 00:05.780
Congrats on being discharged!

00:06.990 --> 00:08.450
Thank you for your help.

00:08.450 --> 00:10.090
How do you feel?

00:10.090 --> 00:12.910
I'm just glad I can finally get out of bed.

00:13.340 --> 00:16.510
The best part is how easy it 
is to go to the bathroom.

00:16.510 --> 00:19.330
How do you use the bathroom?

00:19.330 --> 00:20.650
It's a secret.

00:20.650 --> 00:21.800
You?

00:21.800 --> 00:22.920
It's a secret!

00:24.160 --> 00:25.560
And you?

00:25.560 --> 00:28.080
What exactly is going on 
in this conversation?

00:29.070 --> 00:31.330
Why are you looking at me?

00:31.970 --> 00:33.620
Well, then...

00:33.620 --> 00:34.920
Are you going home?

00:34.920 --> 00:37.260
Even if I wanted to, we're sealed in.

00:38.620 --> 00:42.110
I can't even do my work in this 
situation, so I'll have to...

00:43.530 --> 00:45.670
Alexandra, you have a patient.

00:46.680 --> 00:47.580
My, my.

00:47.580 --> 00:48.980
Are you all right?

00:48.980 --> 00:51.740
She's not feeling well.

00:52.070 --> 00:54.240
I'll have a look over there.

00:54.980 --> 00:56.560
I'll take you to your room.

00:57.940 --> 00:59.930
Oh, thanks.

02:33.930 --> 02:36.590
I'm tired of studying.

02:36.590 --> 02:38.230
Exams are next week.

02:39.170 --> 02:43.630
Lazarus, can you do the nutrition calculations
 for cooking class and check my sewing?

02:43.630 --> 02:44.560
Okay.

02:44.560 --> 02:46.590
Oh! Mine, too!

02:46.590 --> 02:47.440
Mine, too!

02:47.710 --> 02:49.280
Mine too, when you're done.

02:49.800 --> 02:51.310
That's a lot.

02:51.970 --> 02:54.610
Could someone check the sorcerers 
exam material range?

02:54.610 --> 02:55.970
Pass.

02:55.970 --> 02:58.420
I don't want to think 
about history right now.

02:58.420 --> 03:00.240
Same, pass.

03:00.240 --> 03:02.690
I'm completely lost.

03:02.690 --> 03:03.500
Come on.

03:03.870 --> 03:05.770
I can take a look, if that works for you.

03:05.770 --> 03:07.170
That'd be great.

03:07.170 --> 03:09.730
Isaac, could you look at mine, too?

03:09.730 --> 03:10.330
Sure.

03:11.150 --> 03:13.460
Nothing I read is sticking.

03:13.460 --> 03:15.250
I know.

03:15.670 --> 03:19.260
<i>So this is what study groups are like.</i>

03:19.260 --> 03:21.630
I can't blame you if 
you're getting bored.

03:21.630 --> 03:25.900
Normally, we'd be grabbing food in town.

03:25.900 --> 03:27.520
But we can't do that right now.

03:27.520 --> 03:31.500
Yeah, I wanna go check out the new shops.

03:31.500 --> 03:32.400
I want clothes!

03:32.730 --> 03:36.150
The new comics should be out!

03:36.150 --> 03:37.940
Right, there's no signal!

03:38.330 --> 03:41.200
Looks like everyone's stressed out.

03:41.200 --> 03:43.170
I mean...

03:43.170 --> 03:45.400
There's nothing to do but study.

03:47.370 --> 03:50.160
I thought people would
 start saying that, so...

03:50.540 --> 03:52.780
Did you bring us something?!

03:54.310 --> 03:56.070
Here you go.

03:56.070 --> 03:57.540
What are these?

03:57.540 --> 03:58.800
Puzzles?

03:59.960 --> 04:01.340
Do you two not know?

04:01.860 --> 04:04.840
This is a training game for sorcerers.

04:05.750 --> 04:08.430
You put a simple spell on the puzzle,

04:08.870 --> 04:12.280
and you race to see who can solve it first.

04:13.470 --> 04:16.910
It tests your analytic skills and 
ability to manipulate magic power.

04:17.260 --> 04:19.270
That sounds fun.

04:19.270 --> 04:20.740
Magic power, huh?

04:20.740 --> 04:22.790
I don't think I could do it.

04:22.790 --> 04:25.490
Do you not have spells to open locks?

04:25.490 --> 04:27.030
I do, but...

04:27.450 --> 04:30.040
You should try it out.

04:30.040 --> 04:32.360
I guess we could try it out, if you want.

04:32.360 --> 04:35.290
Plus, I want to see your magic again.

04:35.290 --> 04:36.830
True, I'd like to see it, too.

04:38.600 --> 04:39.960
O-Okay.

04:40.830 --> 04:42.770
Okay, first round.

04:42.770 --> 04:44.350
Who wants to lock it?

04:44.600 --> 04:45.780
I'll do it.

04:45.780 --> 04:46.800
Guess I'm in.

04:47.310 --> 04:50.900
Okay, Roy, Sofia, and... 
maybe I'll play, too.

04:51.360 --> 04:53.180
Let's make it a triple this time.

04:56.630 --> 04:58.110
Who's up?

04:58.110 --> 04:58.940
Me!

04:58.940 --> 04:59.430
I'm in.

04:59.430 --> 04:59.980
Yeah.

04:59.980 --> 05:00.850
Why not?

05:01.420 --> 05:02.650
And...

05:04.990 --> 05:07.510
Zoe, Chise, you've never 
played before, right?

05:07.770 --> 05:09.300
You should give it a try.

05:10.090 --> 05:10.900
Okay.

05:11.360 --> 05:12.910
Thanks.

05:16.600 --> 05:17.840
All right, let's go.

05:18.150 --> 05:20.800
Three, two, one.

05:21.180 --> 05:22.050
Start!

05:23.860 --> 05:25.590
Thanks for walking with me.

05:25.980 --> 05:28.660
You can call me if you need anything.

05:31.440 --> 05:34.630
Do people ever tell you that 
you're overprotective?

05:35.570 --> 05:38.200
But humans are so frail.

05:39.080 --> 05:40.690
You're not wrong.

05:41.250 --> 05:46.430
Alexandra gets a notification if there's 
ever anything wrong with my vitals.

05:46.430 --> 05:48.460
I should be all right.

05:49.450 --> 05:52.260
Especially with the intensified security.

05:53.370 --> 05:55.900
Just hope the students
 don't find out too much.

05:56.390 --> 05:57.370
Yeah.

05:57.920 --> 06:00.300
You're right, there are more patrols lately.

06:00.660 --> 06:02.060
See you around.

06:02.060 --> 06:02.740
Yeah.

06:05.230 --> 06:07.330
Do you like music?

06:07.860 --> 06:09.350
Music?

06:09.350 --> 06:11.150
I've never thought about it.

06:11.150 --> 06:12.730
Nor have I heard much.

06:13.920 --> 06:15.140
All right.

06:15.140 --> 06:19.320
I'll try and find something 
you'll like for next time.

06:20.040 --> 06:21.160
Okay.

06:21.780 --> 06:22.730
Thanks.

06:27.880 --> 06:29.910
<i>Music, huh?</i>

06:30.470 --> 06:34.090
<i>I think I remember Angelica playing 
a record quite a while ago.</i>

06:35.540 --> 06:38.730
<i>Chise doesn't seem to listen to music.</i>

06:39.340 --> 06:42.280
<i>I wonder what kind of music she listens to?</i>

06:43.010 --> 06:46.320
<i>She seems to like most food.</i>

06:46.320 --> 06:48.960
<i>She never complains about anything.</i>

06:49.300 --> 06:52.220
<i>But I haven't heard much 
about her preferences.</i>

06:53.440 --> 06:56.940
<i>I wonder what she was 
like before she met me.</i>

06:57.390 --> 06:58.940
<i>I should ask, and...</i>

07:01.310 --> 07:02.360
<i>There she is.</i>

07:05.080 --> 07:06.560
You can do this, Zoe.

07:06.560 --> 07:08.410
Try taking a step back.

07:08.410 --> 07:09.990
Hurry up.

07:13.870 --> 07:15.600
Done!

07:16.080 --> 07:17.560
Who was first?

07:17.560 --> 07:21.180
From the top, Martin, 
Jasmine, Beatrice, Rian.

07:21.180 --> 07:22.790
You're last, Zoe.

07:22.790 --> 07:24.430
Rats!

07:24.430 --> 07:26.550
It's your first time.
Don't be so hard on yourself.

07:26.850 --> 07:29.530
You were never very good at games.

07:29.530 --> 07:31.250
Even though you were technically first.

07:31.540 --> 07:34.330
To think the whole thing 
would open on its own...

07:34.720 --> 07:36.750
Magic sure is something.

07:36.750 --> 07:39.310
You did fall for a trap, though.

07:41.420 --> 07:44.930
I set up a trap that's triggered 
when you force it open.

07:44.930 --> 07:47.490
How long does it last?

07:47.490 --> 07:48.440
Not that long.

07:48.440 --> 07:49.070
Watch.

07:51.810 --> 07:52.780
See?

07:52.780 --> 07:54.870
What are all of you up to?

07:55.960 --> 07:57.420
Veronica!

07:58.160 --> 08:00.280
Just playing games from back in first year.

08:00.280 --> 08:01.390
Wanna join us?

08:01.390 --> 08:02.540
Maybe.

08:05.430 --> 08:06.120
Philomela.

08:10.360 --> 08:12.050
Let's play each other. It's been a while.

08:14.250 --> 08:15.600
I...

08:16.570 --> 08:18.030
Um, you don't have to—

08:18.030 --> 08:19.070
Sounds great.

08:19.540 --> 08:21.900
You're good at this kind of thing.

08:22.770 --> 08:24.600
I'd like to see you do it.

08:26.710 --> 08:29.370
Understood...

08:31.230 --> 08:32.330
You can do this.

08:33.440 --> 08:35.680
This is a pretty interesting match-up.

08:36.260 --> 08:38.370
Well, same rules as before.

08:38.370 --> 08:39.920
The first to solve it wins.

08:40.440 --> 08:41.400
Rian...

08:44.240 --> 08:45.920
<i>Is this going to be all right?</i>

08:47.650 --> 08:49.680
Are you ready?

08:49.680 --> 08:51.260
Ready...

08:51.260 --> 08:52.270
Start!

09:08.680 --> 09:10.100
Alcyone!

09:11.310 --> 09:12.640
Alcyone?

09:13.170 --> 09:14.520
Are you tired?

09:14.520 --> 09:15.670
No.

09:16.180 --> 09:19.450
It seems it took me a while 
to store my memories.

09:19.450 --> 09:20.620
Yeah?

09:23.060 --> 09:24.140
Alcyone.

09:24.970 --> 09:27.340
Could you help make lunch?

09:28.090 --> 09:30.460
I'll take care of Philomela.

09:30.460 --> 09:32.460
Yes, Master.

09:39.300 --> 09:41.970
You're one tireless monster.

09:42.260 --> 09:43.720
You must be tired.

09:44.190 --> 09:45.810
No, ma'am.

09:45.810 --> 09:47.140
How may I help?

09:47.140 --> 09:49.740
Let's see... Could you peel the oranges?

09:49.740 --> 09:51.220
Understood.

09:52.210 --> 09:55.480
We haven't been on a picnic in a while. 
I'm glad the weather held up.

09:55.480 --> 09:56.260
Yes.

09:58.400 --> 10:00.270
Hey, Alcyone...

10:01.210 --> 10:05.650
We can't have cameras or 
albums or photos on us.

10:06.130 --> 10:09.700
So please, store this scene for us.

10:27.790 --> 10:28.940
Hello.

10:29.590 --> 10:30.610
Hi.

10:32.110 --> 10:34.190
<i>That familiar from before.</i>

10:36.170 --> 10:38.760
We've met before.

10:39.390 --> 10:41.990
If you'll pardon the rude question...

10:43.500 --> 10:46.990
Are you of the same kind as me?

10:49.950 --> 10:51.460
The same?

10:51.460 --> 10:53.000
What makes you think that?

10:53.320 --> 10:57.530
I cloak myself in matter
 in order to carry out tasks.

10:58.750 --> 11:01.470
I felt that you may be doing the same.

11:03.740 --> 11:04.950
Elias.

11:05.860 --> 11:07.670
I wonder what they're talking about.

11:08.360 --> 11:12.150
One of the new students called your name.

11:12.670 --> 11:14.140
Are you her caretaker?

11:14.720 --> 11:15.740
No.

11:16.800 --> 11:20.500
I think I'm more the one being taken care of.

11:20.500 --> 11:22.240
It's both, I suppose.

11:22.720 --> 11:25.540
That's quite peculiar.

11:25.540 --> 11:26.570
Peculiar?

11:26.570 --> 11:32.220
We are created to serve those who summon us.

11:33.540 --> 11:35.870
You seem to be independent.

11:36.710 --> 11:39.600
I'm not an artificial fairy.

11:39.600 --> 11:41.800
Pardon me, then.

11:42.300 --> 11:44.000
What brings you here today?

11:44.460 --> 11:46.300
Observation.

11:47.010 --> 11:48.090
<i>What?</i>

11:48.090 --> 11:53.800
My ability to analyze observations 
is not very sophisticated.

11:53.800 --> 11:55.010
I envy you.

11:55.280 --> 11:56.210
No...

11:57.670 --> 12:01.820
<i>I could ignore her, but I keep replying.</i>

12:03.430 --> 12:06.860
There's more that I don't know 
than you give me credit for.

12:07.610 --> 12:08.990
Is that so?

12:13.550 --> 12:17.270
I apologize for my inability 
to maintain a conversation.

12:17.940 --> 12:21.970
I still don't know how

12:24.640 --> 12:26.730
to engage others.

12:30.110 --> 12:32.030
You're both down to your last one!

12:40.150 --> 12:41.830
I lost again!

12:42.280 --> 12:47.120
I think you should try to think deeper 
about things and about others.

12:47.120 --> 12:48.540
Too hard.

12:51.320 --> 12:54.420
Grandmother, Rian and I...

12:55.810 --> 12:57.170
What a waste of time.

12:57.580 --> 13:00.280
You've no need to win at any games.

13:00.920 --> 13:04.820
Spend that time reading your textbooks.

13:04.820 --> 13:07.260
You're already behind everyone else.

13:17.520 --> 13:20.190
Rian won!

13:20.940 --> 13:21.810
He won.

13:26.910 --> 13:28.350
Why did you hold back?

13:29.100 --> 13:29.820
Rian!

13:29.820 --> 13:32.600
I'm atrocious at these games.

13:32.600 --> 13:35.380
There's no way you'd take longer than me!

13:35.380 --> 13:36.380
Stop!

13:36.380 --> 13:37.860
You're getting too worked up, you idiot!

13:40.730 --> 13:43.210
I'm not the same as I was before.

13:43.860 --> 13:47.730
Don't put your expectations on 
me just to be disappointed.

13:49.750 --> 13:51.060
Seriously, Rian!

13:52.580 --> 13:53.510
Wait!

13:53.760 --> 13:55.620
Philomela, are you okay?

13:56.700 --> 13:57.950
I'm sorry.

14:01.660 --> 14:03.560
Sorry, I'll be back.

14:03.560 --> 14:04.540
Chise!

14:05.340 --> 14:06.070
Damn it!

14:07.020 --> 14:09.720
Do those two have some kind of history?

14:09.720 --> 14:12.000
I know they're relatives, but...

14:12.720 --> 14:14.710
I bet it's complicated.

14:15.180 --> 14:16.350
Jasmine?

14:16.350 --> 14:17.360
I...

14:22.300 --> 14:23.390
Rian!

14:27.380 --> 14:30.320
Why doesn't she try to win?!

14:30.960 --> 14:34.460
She's way smarter than me 
and better at sorcery!

14:34.860 --> 14:36.880
Why is she acting so weak?

14:37.950 --> 14:42.240
It's probably the only 
way she could survive.

14:42.490 --> 14:44.090
I don't get it.

14:44.090 --> 14:47.830
Sure, she's never been the assertive type.

14:48.310 --> 14:50.030
But it's only gotten worse!

14:50.030 --> 14:51.370
Why—

14:52.630 --> 14:54.920
Why do you think she <i>needs</i> to be that way?!

14:55.260 --> 14:58.380
Try giving it some thought, you whiner!

15:01.160 --> 15:03.540
You think about other people too much!

15:04.230 --> 15:06.350
At least I'm not arrogant.

15:15.200 --> 15:21.440
I never had friends before I came 
here, so I don't really know...

15:22.130 --> 15:25.170
Is it normal to say and do stuff like that?

15:27.310 --> 15:29.760
Here's how I see it, then.

15:29.760 --> 15:34.380
I don't think it's good to act
 that way toward girls, or friends.

15:38.400 --> 15:39.120
Philomela!

15:41.260 --> 15:43.790
Hey, are you okay?

15:44.170 --> 15:45.330
<i>Is she crying?</i>

15:51.740 --> 15:52.720
<i>That's right.</i>

15:55.360 --> 15:57.270
<i>These eyes don't cry.</i>

15:58.860 --> 16:00.830
<i>I've seen it before.</i>

16:03.910 --> 16:12.600
Rian and I have always competed 
and played games together.

16:13.060 --> 16:15.030
He's honest about his feelings.

16:15.860 --> 16:17.240
So he'd get upset.

16:17.840 --> 16:21.370
But he'd always say good things about me.

16:24.380 --> 16:27.790
But now, I'm not allowed to win...

16:28.630 --> 16:30.800
Yet I'm not allowed to lose, either...

16:31.410 --> 16:33.140
I'm an embarrassment.

16:33.890 --> 16:35.500
I'm worthless.

16:36.320 --> 16:38.610
No matter what I do, I...

16:42.370 --> 16:43.560
Is that...

16:45.160 --> 16:48.210
because that's what your 
grandmother said to you?

16:50.740 --> 16:53.970
What did you want to do?

16:53.970 --> 16:57.150
In the past, back there, and right now.

17:05.210 --> 17:11.880
There's nothing I'm allowed to do.

17:15.700 --> 17:17.200
That's unusual.

17:17.830 --> 17:20.100
I've never seen you at a loss for words.

17:21.060 --> 17:23.320
What should I have said?

17:24.430 --> 17:29.880
<i>Our origins, our circumstances, our 
personalities, and our burdens are different.</i>

17:31.130 --> 17:33.800
<i>And here I am, feeling 
some kind of closeness.</i>

17:35.230 --> 17:37.980
I want to tell her she can do something.

17:40.370 --> 17:45.740
<i>The same way those around me 
have told me that I'm free.</i>

17:46.400 --> 17:47.480
Coming.

17:48.150 --> 17:49.500
Nurse's office.

17:49.740 --> 17:51.840
<i>Alexandra, we're being assembled.</i>

17:53.140 --> 17:55.930
I'm in the middle of something right now.

17:57.650 --> 18:01.540
Doctor, my sister says she's feeling sick.

18:07.090 --> 18:08.780
P-Please...

18:10.030 --> 18:11.070
Give them back.

18:11.510 --> 18:13.650
You've finally returned.

18:13.650 --> 18:17.230
I thought you'd have starved 
to death somewhere by now.

18:17.490 --> 18:18.940
Please give them back.

18:19.830 --> 18:23.250
I can't take this anymore!

18:23.960 --> 18:28.260
Please give me back our... my... children...

18:31.400 --> 18:35.280
You beasts heal quickly.

18:35.280 --> 18:38.180
You recover even after
 I tinker with your insides.

18:39.090 --> 18:43.190
I left you with a minimal sense of self 
so you'd keep yourself out of trouble.

18:43.970 --> 18:45.190
Fine.

18:45.190 --> 18:46.940
I'll give them back.

18:47.320 --> 18:52.300
It should be about time now.

18:58.280 --> 19:00.230
Rian. It's morning.

19:02.820 --> 19:04.650
It's Saturday.

19:07.770 --> 19:11.750
<i>We never used to get into fights.</i>

19:16.740 --> 19:18.310
It's time for rain.

19:23.650 --> 19:26.350
I wonder if it's raining 
outside the College, too.

19:29.420 --> 19:31.040
Do you like the rain?

19:31.040 --> 19:32.600
I suppose.

19:32.950 --> 19:35.490
I'm worried about our crops back home.

19:35.490 --> 19:37.810
We haven't had the pumpkins yet.

19:38.490 --> 19:41.090
We should be back by Christmas.

19:41.810 --> 19:43.480
I don't know if we can finish them all.

19:43.810 --> 19:47.210
Someone might have already harvested them.

19:47.210 --> 19:49.730
Yeah, I bet.

19:50.490 --> 19:52.540
What shall we make with the pumpkins?

19:53.160 --> 19:54.740
Potage, maybe.

19:55.330 --> 19:58.540
Bake them with honey and mustard.

19:58.540 --> 20:02.060
Have Silver bake a cake.

20:02.690 --> 20:03.730
<i>Chise and I...</i>

20:04.800 --> 20:06.300
<i>Elias and I...</i>

20:06.910 --> 20:10.080
<i>...haven't sat down to talk for a while.</i>

20:15.910 --> 20:17.380
Elias.

20:17.380 --> 20:20.690
Is it just me, or am I seeing 
more things than usual?

20:21.240 --> 20:23.470
It's winter, after all.

20:23.470 --> 20:24.830
Is it because it's winter?

20:24.830 --> 20:26.350
Seeing more of what?

20:27.340 --> 20:28.500
Violet.

20:28.500 --> 20:29.990
Am I intruding?

20:29.990 --> 20:31.550
Intruding...

20:31.550 --> 20:33.160
No, it's fine.

20:33.760 --> 20:37.590
Mr. Ainsworth, Jasmine's 
not feeling too well.

20:37.590 --> 20:40.870
She'll probably be absent 
for the next class.

20:41.460 --> 20:43.700
I plan to take care of her.

20:44.350 --> 20:46.990
So you'll both be absent, then.

20:46.990 --> 20:51.770
Oh, and if you're really 
serious about learning magic,

20:51.770 --> 20:54.350
you should find another master.

20:54.890 --> 20:58.060
Becoming a mage versus a sorcerer 
are two different paths.

20:58.060 --> 21:00.320
I figured as much.

21:00.970 --> 21:02.690
I'll give it some thought.

21:03.200 --> 21:05.390
So, what're you seeing a lot of?

21:06.610 --> 21:08.220
Ghosts and stuff?

21:08.220 --> 21:09.700
There's a lot lately.

21:09.700 --> 21:11.960
You can see them, too, Violet?

21:12.250 --> 21:13.480
Sometimes.

21:13.910 --> 21:17.990
Ghosts and apparitions are part of 
life in the winter in this country.

21:17.990 --> 21:20.410
It's the season the dead come back.

21:20.410 --> 21:24.380
Where I'm from, that's in the summer.

21:24.920 --> 21:28.190
We even have a game called "kimodameshi."

21:28.190 --> 21:29.380
Kimodameshi?

21:29.720 --> 21:32.740
I guess it's like a horror tour.

21:32.740 --> 21:36.060
Students wander around school at night 
without supervision, for example.

21:37.530 --> 21:38.840
Have you done it before?

21:38.840 --> 21:40.650
I have, I guess.

21:40.650 --> 21:42.470
Could you tell me more?

21:42.990 --> 21:43.870
Sure.

21:49.550 --> 21:50.690
I see.

21:50.690 --> 21:51.910
I get it.

21:52.520 --> 21:56.460
By the way, I'm super bored right now.

21:56.460 --> 21:59.350
Wanna do something fun together?

22:05.270 --> 22:08.010
I'm seeing a lot of patients lately.

22:08.940 --> 22:11.340
I know it's flu season, but...

22:12.160 --> 22:12.970
Oh?
